      <memberdef kind="function" id="group__HAL__Group1_1gaecac54d350c3730e6831eb404e557dc4" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type><ref refid="stm32h7xx__hal__def_8h_1a63c0679d1cb8b8c684fbb0632743478f" kindref="member">HAL_StatusTypeDef</ref></type>
        <definition>HAL_StatusTypeDef HAL_Init</definition>
        <argsstring>(void)</argsstring>
        <name>HAL_Init</name>
        <param>
          <type>void</type>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>This function is used to initialize the HAL Library; it must be the first instruction to be executed in the main program (before to call any other HAL function), it performs the following: Configures the SysTick to generate an interrupt each 1 millisecond, which is clocked by the HSI (at this stage, the clock is not yet configured and thus the system is running from the internal HSI at 16 MHz). </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Set NVIC Group Priority to 4. Calls the <ref refid="bootstrap_2Core_2Src_2stm32h7xx__hal__msp_8c_1ae4fb8e66865c87d0ebab74a726a6891f" kindref="member">HAL_MspInit()</ref> callback function defined in user file &quot;stm32h7xx_hal_msp.c&quot; to do the global low level hardware initialization</para>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para>SysTick is used as time base for the <ref refid="group__HAL__Group2_1gab1dc1e6b438daacfe38a312a90221330" kindref="member">HAL_Delay()</ref> function, the application need to ensure that the SysTick time base is always set to 1 millisecond to have correct HAL operation. </para>
</simplesect>
<parameterlist kind="retval"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
